  "body": "## What happens\n\nA 2D Chamfer accepts only a closed boundary. An open selection of one or more connected model edges is refused.\n\nThe user cannot chamfer one edge or one section of a solid edge loop without cutting the complete loop.\n\n## Expected\n\n- The Geometry section accepts one or more open edge chains for a 2D Chamfer.\n- Each chain is cut only from its first selected point to its last selected point.\n- Closed face and loop picks keep the current closed-circuit behaviour.\n- The tool enters and leaves each open chain safely.\n- Stock simulation credits only the selected edge segments.\n- The operation keeps the current tool, cone, flute length, side, and wall checks.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A motion test pins a 2D Chamfer path along one open chain and leaves the chain open.\n- An app test generates a 2D Chamfer from one selected edge.\n- A test covers connected selected edges as one chain and separate chains as separate passes.\n- The verification test credits the selected break and does not credit the unselected loop segments.\n- The quick gate and the reached heavy lanes pass.\n\n## Related\n\nThis is the partial ride left out of #2887. It enables the picked-edge workaround named by that issue. Issue #2930 tracks the remaining-sharp-edge note after this behaviour exists.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Chamfer can now machine one or more selected open edge chains without cutting the complete edge loop.\r\n",
